  "explanation": "<strong>Step 1: Understand the subquery</strong><br>The first subquery selects all course numbers ($cNo$) from the <code>Course</code> table where $dNo = \\text{\"D01\"}$.<br>From the table, the courses belonging to department $D01$ are: $\\{C11, C12\\}$.<br><br><strong>Step 2: Understand the EXCEPT and NOT EXIST condition</strong><br>For each student tuple $S$ in <code>Student</code>, the inner query computes:<br>$\\text{Result} = \\{C11, C12\\} \\setminus \\{cNo \\mid \\text{Student } S \\text{ is registered for } cNo\\}$.<br><br>The condition <code>NOT EXIST</code> evaluates to <strong>TRUE</strong> if and only if this $\\text{Result}$ set is empty $(\\emptyset)$, meaning student $S$ has registered for <strong>all</strong> courses offered by department $D01$.<br><br><strong>Step 3: Evaluate for each student in the table</strong><br>1. <strong>S01</strong>: Registered for $\\{C11, C12\\}$.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$\\{C11, C12\\} \\setminus \\{C11, C12\\} = \\emptyset \\implies$ <strong>TRUE</strong>.<br>2. <strong>S02</strong>: Registered for $\\{C11\\}$.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$\\{C11, C12\\} \\setminus \\{C11\\} = \\{C12\\} \\neq \\emptyset \\implies$ FALSE.<br>3. <strong>S03</strong>: Registered for $\\{C21, C22, C23\\}$.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$\\{C11, C12\\} \\setminus \\{C21, C22, C23\\} = \\{C11, C12\\} \\neq \\emptyset \\implies$ FALSE.<br>4. <strong>S04</strong>: Registered for $\\{C11, C12\\}$.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$\\{C11, C12\\} \\setminus \\{C11, C12\\} = \\emptyset \\implies$ <strong>TRUE</strong>.<br>5. <strong>S05</strong>: Registered for $\\{C11, C21\\}$.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$\\{C11, C12\\} \\setminus \\{C11, C21\\} = \\{C12\\} \\neq \\emptyset \\implies$ FALSE.<br><br><strong>Conclusion:</strong><br>The query returns $2$ rows (corresponding to students <strong>S01</strong> and <strong>S04</strong>).",
